{"title": "SENSING Astra S56", "parts": {"header": "<div class=sd><div class=sd-grid><div class=sd-head><a class=sd-maker href=\"https://www.sensing-world.com/en/\">SENSING TECH</a><h1 id=\"_top\">SENSING Astra S56</h1><p class=sd-type>Stereo camera: wide-angle global-shutter cameras with a 400 Hz IMU</p><p class=sd-chips><span class=\"cl cam unk\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"1.5\" y=\"4\" width=\"13\" height=\"9\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"2.6\"/><path d=\"M5.5 4l1-1.6h3l1 1.6\"/></svg><span class=t>Camera not known</span></span><span class=\"cl imu unk\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"4\" y=\"4\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" rx=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M6.5 4V2M9.5 4V2M6.5 14v-2M9.5 14v-2M4 6.5H2M4 9.5H2M14 6.5h-2M14 9.5h-2\"/></svg><span class=t>IMU not known</span></span></p></div><figure class=sd-plate><div class=sd-frame><img src=\"/media/sensors/astra-s56/astra-s56.jpg\" alt=\"Placeholder for the Astra S56 photo\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\"></div><figcaption><a href=\"https://www.sensing-world.com/en/h-col-132.html\">Placeholder: photo pending</a></figcaption></figure><div class=sd-cta><div class=sd-buttons><a class=\"sd-btn primary\" href=\"https://www.sensing-world.com/en/h-col-132.html\">SENSING stereo cameras</a><a class=sd-btn href=\"#specifications\">All specs (9)</a></div></div><div class=sd-specs><dl class=sd-rows><div class=sd-row><dt>Cameras</dt><dd>1 of 2 recorded: 2560 × 1984 at 20 Hz<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Shutter</dt><dd>Global<a class=sd-tag href=\"https://www.sensing-world.com/en/h-col-132.html\">Maker</a></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Field of view</dt><dd>Calibrated 154° × 116°<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span><br>130° or 140° horizontal<a class=sd-tag href=\"https://www.sensing-world.com/en/h-col-132.html\">Maker</a></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Baseline</dt><dd>One camera in this run<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>IMU</dt><dd>400 Hz<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Output</dt><dd>GMSL2; ROS 1 bag in the recording<a class=sd-tag href=\"https://www.sensing-world.com/en/h-col-132.html\">Maker</a></dd></div></dl><p class=sd-foot>Maker values from the SENSING product pages, read 2026-11-20 · 1 recording, 58 s</p></div></div></div>", "glance": "<p>Wide-angle stereo camera from SENSING TECH with two 5 MP global-shutter sensors and a 6-axis IMU, on a GMSL2 link. One recording from the maker in front of a lit AprilGrid in a dark room, with one of the two cameras, solved as camera + IMU. These are first results; the stereo pair is not calibrated yet.</p><div class=band><div class=\"demo empty\"><b>No video on this page.</b> The values below come from the solved run.</div><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.31<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>+3.91<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>23.7<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div><p class=sd-note>Reprojection is how far, in pixels, the detected corners lie from where the solve puts them. td is the camera–IMU time offset, and the lever arm is the camera–IMU position offset.</p><p class=sd-note>First results from one recording. There is no second recording, no maker calibration and no round-trip check to compare with yet.</p>", "process": "<p>The path of the rig around the board, as MVIS solved it. To explore it:</p><ul class=list><li>Press <b>Play</b> or drag the bar to follow the path.</li><li>Use the <b>view buttons</b> to change the view.</li><li>Pick a <b>camera card</b> to put that camera on the frustum, the pyramid that shows its view.</li></ul><p>Each card draws the board from the solved pose, with the corners MVIS detected. We publish no camera images.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=proc-wrap><button type=button class=proc-open hidden><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 220\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"217.2,157.4 322.2,196.5 322.9,59.2 218.0,20.0 217.2,157.4\" fill=\"var(--strong)\" fill-opacity=\".1\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\"/><polyline points=\"97.3,166.0 97.3,166.0 97.3,166.0 97.3,166.0 97.3,166.0 97.3,166.1 97.3,166.1 97.3,166.1 97.3,166.1 97.3,166.1 97.3,166.0 97.3,165.9 97.2,166.0 97.2,165.9 97.2,165.9 97.3,165.9 97.2,165.9 97.2,165.9 97.2,165.8 97.3,165.8 102.0,161.0 121.7,145.4 150.6,132.4 181.0,128.3 197.3,129.0 201.1,129.4 201.0,129.4 193.2,128.7 167.5,129.1 136.9,137.3 114.4,150.4 99.3,163.5 97.2,165.7 97.3,165.5 103.7,159.4 125.4,143.1 154.9,131.2 180.2,128.3 198.6,129.1 201.1,129.4 200.8,129.4 190.6,128.5 163.2,129.7 132.8,139.2 111.4,152.9 98.5,164.4 97.2,165.8 97.9,165.4 107.1,159.9 121.5,150.7 127.7,145.0 128.9,143.0 128.9,143.0 124.7,144.1 108.5,151.1 100.1,162.8 107.0,174.2 122.8,181.3 148.9,184.7 173.1,182.5 181.5,180.2 181.8,180.1 179.9,180.7 164.2,183.9 141.8,184.4 117.1,179.5 102.3,169.7 101.8,157.8 115.9,147.3 127.9,143.3 128.9,143.1 128.5,143.2 118.7,146.1 103.1,155.9 101.2,167.9 113.9,178.1 137.4,184.0 160.1,184.4 178.6,181.1 181.8,180.2 181.7,180.2 175.8,181.9 153.6,184.7 126.9,182.3 109.6,176.0 100.2,165.0 105.9,153.1 122.5,144.8 128.8,143.0 129.3,143.0 137.3,143.6 155.1,148.3 156.4,165.8 153.1,175.2 153.0,175.2 155.5,167.0 155.2,145.1 143.3,130.5 120.8,122.3 110.8,120.8 110.5,120.8 117.1,121.6 138.8,127.9 154.9,144.1 156.3,163.1 153.2,174.7 153.0,175.3 154.6,170.5 156.5,150.2 144.5,131.3 125.7,123.2 111.6,120.9 110.4,120.8 113.9,121.2 132.9,125.4 152.2,139.1 156.5,161.2 153.7,173.5 153.0,175.3 153.8,173.0 156.9,156.1 149.0,135.1 127.6,123.9 112.0,120.9 110.4,120.8 111.8,120.9 126.4,123.6 148.1,134.2 156.9,154.9 153.9,172.6 153.0,175.4 152.8,175.3 145.3,173.6 123.7,169.6 102.9,166.6 97.3,165.9 97.1,165.9 94.8,167.9 88.2,177.5 86.0,188.2 86.1,190.6 86.1,190.6 84.2,190.1 78.3,185.0 77.1,177.2 82.3,169.4 87.6,167.4 88.3,167.3 88.3,167.3 84.8,168.0 79.3,172.2 77.1,181.6 82.0,189.0 85.9,190.6 86.2,190.6 85.7,190.5 81.0,188.2 77.1,181.6 79.3,172.3 85.8,167.8 88.3,167.4 88.4,167.3 88.8,167.7 91.1,169.0 95.0,177.0 100.1,196.7 101.7,199.6 101.8,199.7 101.5,199.8 98.7,199.8 97.1,195.5 100.9,185.4 107.5,177.0 110.5,174.8 110.7,174.7 110.3,174.9 106.2,178.2 100.5,185.9 97.1,195.8 99.5,200.0 101.6,199.6 101.7,199.6 101.2,199.8 98.0,199.2 97.4,193.8 102.2,183.4 108.6,176.1 110.7,174.7 110.7,174.7 110.5,173.0 108.1,167.7 101.1,164.7 97.5,165.7 97.3,165.8 97.2,165.8 97.2,165.8 97.3,165.9 97.3,165.9 97.2,166.0 97.3,166.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg><span>Explore in 3D (about 1 MB)</span></button><div class=\"mvv\" data-mvv=\"scene\" data-mode=\"site\" data-src=\"/media/sensors/astra-s56/views0.json\"></div></div></div>", "rig": "<p>The solved rig in 3D, to scale. Tap a sensor to see its values. In full screen you can rotate and zoom. Grid squares are 20 mm.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><h3 class=rig-h>To scale, from above and the front</h3><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=rig-c><div class=rig-views><figure class=rig-view><figcaption>From above</figcaption><svg viewBox=\"0 0 420 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"From above: solved camera and IMU layout, to scale\"><line class=lever x1=\"351.9\" y1=\"328.0\" x2=\"210.0\" y2=\"175.7\"/><path d=\"M210.0 175.7L66.2 142.2A147.7 147.7 0 0 1 353.8 142.2Z\" fill=\"var(--accent)\" fill-opacity=\".12\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-opacity=\".7\"/><g class=cam transform=\"translate(210.0 175.7) rotate(0.0)\"><rect x=\"-11\" y=\"-3\" width=\"22\" height=\"9\" rx=\"2.5\" fill=\"var(--accent)\"/><rect x=\"-4.5\" y=\"-6\" width=\"9\" height=\"4\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"var(--accent)\"/></g><rect class=imu x=\"346.9\" y=\"323.0\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" rx=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"351.9\" y1=\"328.0\" x2=\"316.8\" y2=\"328.0\" stroke=\"var(--y)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"351.9\" y1=\"328.0\" x2=\"352.0\" y2=\"363.2\" stroke=\"var(--z)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text class=\"axis\" x=\"306.8\" y=\"332.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"fill:var(--y);font-weight:700\">y</text><text class=\"axis\" x=\"352.0\" y=\"377.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"fill:var(--z);font-weight:700\">z</text><text class=\"dim\" x=\"210.0\" y=\"199.7\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cam0</text><text class=\"dim\" x=\"281.0\" y=\"255.8\" text-anchor=\"middle\">23.7 mm</text><line class=sc x1=\"230.2\" y1=\"408.0\" x2=\"406\" y2=\"408.0\"/><text class=sct x=\"318.1\" y=\"402.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20 mm</text></svg></figure><figure class=rig-view><figcaption>From the front</figcaption><svg viewBox=\"0 0 420 126\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"From the front: solved camera and IMU layout, to scale\"><circle class=cam cx=\"281.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"281.0\" cy=\"44.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"var(--accent)\"/><rect class=imu x=\"134.0\" y=\"45.4\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" rx=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"139.0\" y1=\"50.4\" x2=\"139.1\" y2=\"15.2\" stroke=\"var(--x)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"139.0\" y1=\"50.4\" x2=\"174.2\" y2=\"50.5\" stroke=\"var(--y)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text class=\"axis\" x=\"184.2\" y=\"54.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" style=\"fill:var(--y);font-weight:700\">y</text><text class=\"dim\" x=\"281.0\" y=\"68.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cam0</text><line class=sc x1=\"230.2\" y1=\"114.4\" x2=\"406\" y2=\"114.4\"/><text class=sct x=\"318.1\" y=\"108.4\" text-anchor=\"middle\">20 mm</text></svg></figure></div></div><div class=\"scroll rig-table\"><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Camera</th><th>Lever x, y, z (mm)</th><th>Distance (mm)</th><th>log(R) (rad)</th><th>td (ms)</th><th>Field of view</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>cam0</th><td>+0.9, +16.1, −17.3</td><td>23.7</td><td>[−2.215, +2.220, −0.009]</td><td>+3.91</td><td>154° × 116°</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class=rig-note>Solved by MVIS. Lever arms (camera–IMU position offsets) are in the IMU frame. Rotation is log(R), camera in the IMU frame.</p>", "detail": "<details class=fold id=\"lens\"><summary>Lens <span>Calibrated field of view</span></summary><div><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><p>Calibrated field of view, horizontal × vertical. cam0: 154° × 116°, corners reach 88° from the axis</p><div class=chart><svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 260\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Image radius against ray angle for each camera\"><line class=g x1=54.0 x2=54.0 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=54.0 y=236 text-anchor=middle>0°</text><line class=g x1=136.3 x2=136.3 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=136.3 y=236 text-anchor=middle>15°</text><line class=g x1=218.7 x2=218.7 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=218.7 y=236 text-anchor=middle>30°</text><line class=g x1=301.0 x2=301.0 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=301.0 y=236 text-anchor=middle>45°</text><line class=g x1=383.3 x2=383.3 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=383.3 y=236 text-anchor=middle>60°</text><line class=g x1=465.7 x2=465.7 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=465.7 y=236 text-anchor=middle>75°</text><line class=g x1=548.0 x2=548.0 y1=12 y2=220 /><text x=548.0 y=236 text-anchor=middle>90°</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=220.0 y2=220.0 /><text x=48 y=224.0 text-anchor=end>0.0</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=168.0 y2=168.0 /><text x=48 y=172.0 text-anchor=end>0.4</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=116.0 y2=116.0 /><text x=48 y=120.0 text-anchor=end>0.8</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=64.0 y2=64.0 /><text x=48 y=68.0 text-anchor=end>1.2</text><line class=g x1=54 x2=548 y1=12.0 y2=12.0 /><text x=48 y=16.0 text-anchor=end>1.6</text><text x=307.0 y=254 text-anchor=middle>Ray angle from the optical axis</text><text x=12 y=110.0 text-anchor=middle transform=\"rotate(-90 12 110.0)\">Image radius / f</text><polyline class=\"c0\" points=\"54.0,220.0 70.5,213.2 86.9,206.4 103.4,199.6 119.9,192.8 136.3,186.1 152.8,179.3 169.3,172.6 185.7,166.0 202.2,159.3 218.7,152.7 235.1,146.2 251.6,139.6 268.1,133.2 284.5,126.8 301.0,120.4 317.5,114.1 333.9,107.8 350.4,101.7 366.9,95.5 383.3,89.5 399.8,83.5 416.3,77.7 432.7,71.9 449.2,66.2 465.7,60.7 482.1,55.3 498.6,50.0 515.1,45.0 531.5,40.1 548.0,35.5\"/></svg></div></div><p class=legend><i class=c0></i>cam0 </p><p class=note>We read these from the calibrated lens fit at the image edges, through the principal point (where the optical axis meets the image). ~ marks an axis past where the corners reached, so the fit is extrapolated there. Past the fit means an edge lies beyond where the fit holds, so we give no value.</p></div></details><details class=fold id=\"imu\" open><summary>IMU <span>Gyro–accel time offset t_ga +3.11 ms</span></summary><div><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><p>Each bar shows a scale as its deviation from 1. IMU model: calyx. <code>t_ga</code>, the time offset between the gyroscope and accelerometer channels: +3.11 ± 0.08 ms.</p><div class=bars><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale x</span><i><u style=\"left:48.91%;width:1.09%\"></u></i><b>−0.18 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale y</span><i><u style=\"left:50.00%;width:0.84%\"></u></i><b>+0.13 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Gyro scale z</span><i><u style=\"left:47.24%;width:2.76%\"></u></i><b>−0.44 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale x</span><i><u style=\"left:46.69%;width:3.31%\"></u></i><b>−0.53 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale y</span><i><u style=\"left:48.96%;width:1.04%\"></u></i><b>−0.17 %</b></div><div class=bar><span>Accel scale z</span><i><u style=\"left:49.57%;width:0.43%\"></u></i><b>−0.07 %</b></div><div class=bar><span></span><em><s>−8 %</s><s>0</s><s>+8 %</s></em><b></b></div></div></div></div></details><details class=fold id=\"timing\" open><summary>Timing <span>cam0 td +3.91 ms</span></summary><div><p>The time offsets, to scale. td is the camera–IMU time offset, with t_imu = t_cam + td.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=chart><svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 102\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Time offsets in milliseconds, to scale\"><line class=\"g\" x1=70.0 x2=70.0 y1=4 y2=78 /><text x=70.0 y=94 text-anchor=middle>-10 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=177.5 x2=177.5 y1=4 y2=78 /><text x=177.5 y=94 text-anchor=middle>-5 ms</text><line class=\"g z\" x1=285.0 x2=285.0 y1=4 y2=78 /><text x=285.0 y=94 text-anchor=middle>+0 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=392.5 x2=392.5 y1=4 y2=78 /><text x=392.5 y=94 text-anchor=middle>+5 ms</text><line class=\"g\" x1=500.0 x2=500.0 y1=4 y2=78 /><text x=500.0 y=94 text-anchor=middle>+10 ms</text><text x=0 y=22>cam0 td</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=369.1 y1=18 y2=18 /><circle class=dot cx=369.1 cy=18 r=5 /><text x=378.1 y=22 text-anchor=start>+3.91</text><text x=0 y=56>t_ga</text><line class=stem x1=285.0 x2=351.8 y1=52 y2=52 /><circle class=dot cx=351.8 cy=52 r=5 /><text x=360.8 y=56 text-anchor=start>+3.11</text></svg></div></div></div></details><details class=fold id=\"full-results\"><summary>Full results <span>Every solved parameter</span></summary><div><p>Rotation is log(R) in rad, camera in the IMU frame.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>MVIS</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>cam0</th></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>1022.47</td></tr><tr><td>fy px</td><td>1022.34</td></tr><tr><td>cx px</td><td>1279.08</td></tr><tr><td>cy px</td><td>985.15</td></tr><tr><td>k1</td><td>−0.04387</td></tr><tr><td>k2</td><td>0.00872</td></tr><tr><td>k3</td><td>−0.00300</td></tr><tr><td>k4</td><td>0.00010</td></tr><tr><td>Lever x mm</td><td>+0.90</td></tr><tr><td>Lever y mm</td><td>+16.14</td></tr><tr><td>Lever z mm</td><td>−17.33</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−2.2152, +2.2199, −0.0094]</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>+3.913</td></tr><tr><td>Reprojection px</td><td>0.422</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>IMU</th></tr><tr><td>t_ga ms</td><td>+3.11 ± 0.08</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></details>", "limits": "<ul class=list><li>First results from one recording. There is no second recording, no maker calibration and no round-trip check to compare with yet.</li><li>The recording holds one of the two cameras, so the stereo extrinsics and the baseline are not calibrated.</li><li>The tag size, 88 mm, is assumed: the maker has not given the board size. The metric scale from the IMU agrees with it to about 0.1 %. It scales the lever arm.</li><li>The images are JPEG-compressed, which can shift detected corners slightly.</li><li>The recording site is assumed to be Shenzhen, the maker&#x27;s city.</li></ul>", "specifications": "<div class=scroll><table class=spec-table><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>Published by the maker</th></tr><tr><td>Maker</td><td>SENSING TECH (Shenzhen)</td></tr><tr><td>Cameras</td><td>2 × 5 MP global shutter, 2560 × 1984 at 30 fps</td></tr><tr><td>Shutter</td><td>Global</td></tr><tr><td>Lens</td><td>Wide angle, 130° or 140° horizontal by variant (S56, S56x)</td></tr><tr><td>IMU chip</td><td>Not published</td></tr><tr><td>Link</td><td>GMSL2</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=2>Measured in these recordings</th></tr><tr><td>Images in the recording</td><td>1 camera, 2560 × 1984 colour at 20 Hz, JPEG</td></tr><tr><td>IMU</td><td>6-axis, gyro and accelerometer at 400 Hz</td></tr><tr><td>Calibrated field of view</td><td>cam0 154° × 116°</td></tr></tbody></table></div>", "run": "<ul class=list><li>Camera with the IMU in one solve. Kannala-Brandt (kb4) fisheye intrinsics seeded from a single-camera solve of the same recording and left free; the camera time offset, IMU scale and misalignment and the gyro-to-accel offset t_ga estimated. Every board corner is used. IMU noise is the noise measured at rest i